<emu-clause id="formal-forin">
  <h1>Enumerating object properties</h1>
  <p>EnumerateObjectProperties's iterator as a host strategy: the host picks each internal method call of the enumeration and each key it returns from the results of the calls before it.</p>

  <emu-primitive id="prim-forinstep" name="ForInStep">
    <emu-signature>ForInStep(_obj_: an Object, _history_: a List of Records): a Record</emu-signature>
    <p>The host's next action in enumerating the properties of _obj_, given _history_, a Record { [[Action]], [[Result]] } for each action so far, in order: the action and the result of the internal method call it made, or ~empty~ for a key it returned. The action is a new Record { [[Kind]], [[Object]], [[Key]] }: [[Kind]] is ~own-property-keys~ (call [[OwnPropertyKeys]] of [[Object]]), ~get-own-property~ (call [[GetOwnProperty]] of [[Object]] with [[Key]]), ~get-prototype-of~ (call [[GetPrototypeOf]] of [[Object]]), ~yield~ (return the String [[Key]]) or ~done~ (the enumeration is over); fields an action does not use are ~empty~. The actions conform to the rules of EnumerateObjectProperties.</p>
  </emu-primitive>

  <emu-reading clause="sec-enumerate-object-properties" steps="1" hashes="bd4a83c385b05ede6d89516758091bd48888c33185749a0ea3f5b220875d8415">
    <emu-alg reading="definition">
      1. Let _history_ be a new empty List.
      1. Let _closure_ be a new Abstract Closure with no parameters that captures _obj_ and _history_ and performs the following steps when called:
        1. Repeat,
          1. Let _action_ be ForInStep(_obj_, _history_).
          1. If _action_.[[Kind]] is ~done~, return CreateIteratorResultObject(*undefined*, *true*).
          1. If _action_.[[Kind]] is ~yield~, then
            1. Append the Record { [[Action]]: _action_, [[Result]]: ~empty~ } to _history_.
            1. Return CreateIteratorResultObject(_action_.[[Key]], *false*).
          1. Let _O_ be _action_.[[Object]].
          1. Let _result_ be ~empty~.
          1. If _action_.[[Kind]] is ~own-property-keys~, set _result_ to ? _O_.[[OwnPropertyKeys]]().
          1. Else if _action_.[[Kind]] is ~get-own-property~, set _result_ to ? _O_.[[GetOwnProperty]](_action_.[[Key]]).
          1. Else,
            1. Assert: _action_.[[Kind]] is ~get-prototype-of~.
            1. Set _result_ to ? _O_.[[GetPrototypeOf]]().
          1. Append the Record { [[Action]]: _action_, [[Result]]: _result_ } to _history_.
      1. Let _next_ be CreateBuiltinFunction(_closure_, 0, *"next"*, « »).
      1. Let _iterator_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(*null*).
      1. Perform ! CreateDataPropertyOrThrow(_iterator_, *"next"*, _next_).
      1. Return _iterator_.
    </emu-alg>
    <emu-note>
      <p>The iterator is never directly accessible, so its [[Prototype]] is unobservable; its `throw` and `return` methods are never invoked, so it has none. The host chooses each internal method call, which the closure makes, so a call that returns an abrupt completion returns it from `next`.</p>
    </emu-note>
  </emu-reading>
</emu-clause>
